The fixture of `overlapping-globs-yield-one-row-per-slug` with the two globs swapped: `alpha`
now comes back as the flat file, so glob order alone decides which file claims a slug.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/alpha/index.md --
---
title: Alpha directory
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/alpha.md --
---
title: Alpha flat
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/mid.md --
---
title: Mid
---

body
-- cmd --
booping query --glob 'plans/*.md' --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --columns title
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
| title | path | slug |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Alpha flat | plans/alpha.md | alpha |
| Mid | plans/mid.md | mid |
-- stderr --
